{"skill":{"slug":"6551-twitter-to-binance-square","displayName":"Twitter To Binance Square"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1772884514763,"changelog":"Initial release of the Twitter to Binance Square Auto-Mirror Skill.\n\n- Automatically fetches and transforms tweets from specified Twitter accounts, hashtags, or keywords.\n- Posts transformed tweets to Binance Square, with support for deduplication and configurable intervals.\n- Provides robust content transformation (translation, hashtag management, tool/source attribution).\n- Includes a flexible JSON configuration schema and state file for managing posted tweets.\n- Supports command-based invocation for easy automation.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3881,"sha256":"c0fcaab6a431f3ed732f03cd9dfa063cdb866e5592113df2150eabbd27c5ff93","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":12451,"sha256":"029d62420556f5ea3e1b734a0e0ebe8e12b1a5e0b783c2c2893bfe352c412fec","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"mirror_config.example.json","size":550,"sha256":"0be30ca1ff967038f7ae3d251030f825fda04afe44b6986db1e869448eb28fcf","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","size":21441,"sha256":"53371f2d7d92565a8691f0a9e0ed248591840f39519d30bf997dc24ce51446d5","contentType":"text/plain"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789111974052,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"89e14ac0132c600ca01c1a1837fed1bd831e1accd375bffb527bf16e914b7891","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/89e14ac0132c600ca01c1a1837fed1bd831e1accd375bffb527bf16e914b7891","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780089793497},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":15,"checkedAt":1789111974052},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is mostly coherent, but it can automatically publish to your Binance Square account and its default safeguards are not strong enough for that authority.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, environment credentials, file state, and Bash execution are expected for this automation, but they combine into credentialed public posting with broad script execution rather than a narrower integration interface.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No package install or dependency chain is present; the artifact is a Markdown skill plus a Python standard-library script. The README does, however, show credentials inline in a cron command, which is weak secret-handling guidance.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill promises a first-post preview and confirmation in SKILL.md, but the script only previews when dry_run is explicitly enabled and mirror_config.example.json sets dry_run to false. The default post template also adds promotional tool attribution to user-published posts.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The state file is disclosed and proportionate for deduplication, and nohup/cron are documented as optional. Still, background or scheduled operation with live posting authority is material and should require careful user control.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose matches the main capability: fetch Twitter/X content through the 6551 API, transform it, and publish it to Binance Square. The concern is that this is high-impact public account posting, defaults to live posting, and can repeat continuously.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Run in dry-run mode first, disable show_tool_attribution unless you explicitly want that text in every post, avoid inline credentials in cron or shell history, and use dedicated least-privilege keys. Do not run it as a background or scheduled job until you are comfortable with the exact accounts, search terms, posting limits, and transformed output it will publish.","findings":"[LP1] expected: The script reads environment credentials, writes a local state file, and makes network requests; those capabilities are consistent with the disclosed mirroring workflow, though the permission surface is broad because Bash is allowed.\n[SQP-2] expected: External transfer of fetched content and account-linked publishing are core to the skill, but the artifact under-explains privacy/account impact and gives weak guidance for long-lived credentials.\n[RA2] expected: State persistence and optional nohup/cron operation are disclosed and useful for deduplication and automation; the concern is user awareness and control over a long-running poster, not hidden persistence.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The auto-run phrases are related to the purpose but broad for a skill that can start credentialed external posting automation.\n[SDI-2] expected: Bash usage is consistent with the included script and curl examples, but it is broader than a scoped API-only interface for posting automation.\n[E1] expected: Calls to ai.6551.io and binance.com are expected and documented for fetching tweets and posting to Binance Square.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: The zh translation default may surprise users, but translation is disabled by default and the script does not appear to implement translation behavior.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The artifact documents translation options, but the script does not use them in content transformation; this is a functional/documentation mismatch rather than evidence of malicious behavior.\n[T01] unexpected: The default 6551 promotional attribution is artifact-backed and materially affects posts made under the user's Binance identity; it is disclosed and toggleable, so this supports Review rather than malicious classification.\n[T09] unexpected: The documented first-post confirmation is not implemented in the executable path, and default configuration can post live without that approval gate.\n[T09] unexpected: The cron example encourages inline API credentials, which increases exposure risk for the 6551 token and Binance Square API key.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789111974052}}}}}